Held at 6.0.0 rather than 5.5.0 because of the IME fix in 52e8a75e: 5.5.0's
CompositionHelper records the end of the composed text only from the timer
compositionupdate schedules, so a typist fast enough to commit the next
syllable before that timer runs loses the syllable in between. Korean commits
a syllable every two or three keystrokes, so the loss is continuous rather
than occasional. tests/web/composition_check.js pins it.
